-- hx-p2p-livestream: the hyperactivity.ai P2P dataflow, as bytes, to an H.264 livestream.
-- Subscribe: GET /api/p2p/signal (the mesh's rendezvous mailbox, every peer's hello/offer/answer)
-- with no id, so the read writes nothing and evicts no peer. Each byte is one 8-bit grey sample of
-- a 64x64 frame (4096 bytes a frame); ffmpeg encodes H.264 + AAC and pushes FLV to HX_LIVE_OUT
-- (rtmp://live.restream.io/live/<key>, or a file). Bytes cross a pipe made here (pipe2) whose read
-- end ffmpeg inherits as pipe:<fd>.
import "host.hypercubical"

